  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Round tables northern regions of Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the Northern and Northwestern regions of Zambia, round tables are established in which relevant stakeholders, like government, donors, private sector, NGOs and knowledge institutes, are invited to brainstorm about the integral development of these regions and how to tap into resources available. Currently, there are a lot of separate initiatives that are not linked to each other. There are opportunities for more coherence in the economic development that comes with mining in the Northern region and the extension of the harbour in the Northwestern region. The Netherlands has several instruments available and a private sector willing to engage.</narrative>
  </description>
